{"step_index":480,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T20:13:58Z","thinking":"**Investigating Displayed Loading Message**\n\nThe API returns data, yet the screen shows \"Loading your history records...\". Observed the user's screenshot; the dropdown filter is set to \"Purchases Only\". The table displays \"Loading your history records...\" even after data retrieval, which suggests a possible client-side rendering issue related to the applied filter. This indicates data might be retrieved but not displayed due to filter.\n\n\n**Examining Initial HTML & Script Flow**\n\nObserved that the initial HTML displays a loading message. The `loadCustomerHistory()` function is triggered after the DOM loads, fetching data based on the selected filter. If data retrieval is successful, the table content is updated. The default loading message seems to persist even when data is available. This implies that the table is not always being updated after the initial fetch, or the update is conditional.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"grep_search","args":{"MatchPerLine":"true","Query":"\"function formatDate\"","SearchPath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\medcheck-bd\\\\client\"","toolAction":"\"Find formatDate definition\"","toolSummary":"\"Find formatDate in client scripts\""}}]}
